-- title:
--   Pole charts of j and j(q^q) over a level field
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'\neq 0$ an integer with $q\nmid M'$, and assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the $\mathbb Q$-subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by `divisorExpansions M'`) is contained in the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $K_1$ an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$; $k_0$ acts on `fieldBar q M'` through the constants. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants is everything; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum $T'$ of $k_0(K')$ with $F_0$ satisfying $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ has all $a_i=0$; and $F_0$ contains every element whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb`. Write $T_1$ for the compositum of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$ with $F_0$, and endow $T_1$ with an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map agrees with the inclusion of $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ into the constants of `fieldBar q M'`. Let $j_1\in T_1$ be nonzero with image in `fieldBar q M'` the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image of `jq`. Then there is $j'\in T_1$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of `qExpand ℚ q jq` (the series obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $q$) such that, writing $B=$ `chartAlgInf A₁ T₁ j₁` and $B'=$ `chartAlgInf A₁ T₁ j'` for the subalgebras of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, respectively $A_1[j'^{-1}]$: for every $y\in B'$ there is $a\in B$ with $s=1+j_1^{-1}a\in B$ and $sy\in B$, and symmetrically for every $y\in B$ there is $a\in B'$ with $s=1+j'^{-1}a\in B'$ and $sy\in B'$.
--
--   This is the level-field form of the comparison, at the cusps, of the pole charts of the two-chart integral models attached to $j$ and to $j(q^q)$: the two integral closures dominate each other after multiplication by elements congruent to $1$ modulo the local uniformiser $j^{-1}$, which come from the modular equation relating $j$ and $j(q^q)$. It is used in the descent arguments on the two-chart integral model over the level field, namely in the results on centred points and on the action of the level automorphisms `levelAutBar` on such points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_qExpand_forall_mem_chartAlgInf_exists_mul_mem_levelField.lean

